{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Content-DPR Response Header.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Content-DPR Response Header.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"content dpr response header content dpr response header","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Content-DPR Response Header.md","fileName":"Content-DPR Response Header.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Content-DPR Response Header","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-28 04:01\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Adaptive Image Delivery and Caching]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Adaptive Image Delivery and Caching","Device-Pixel-Ratio Client Hint","highperformanceimages.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Content-DPR Response Header.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Content-DPR Response Header.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"content dpr response header content dpr response header","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Content-DPR Response Header.md","fileName":"Content-DPR Response Header.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Content-DPR Response Header","heading":"Content-DPR Response Header","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"When an image service returns a representation at a density different from the density implied by the request, Content-DPR can communicate the density actually selected in the response model described by the book.\n\nThat feedback lets the client calculate the image’s intrinsic CSS dimensions consistently instead of treating physical pixels as one-to-one CSS pixels. It is particularly relevant when the server deliberately reduces density for bandwidth or memory reasons. See [[Device-Pixel-Ratio Client Hint]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Adaptive Image Delivery and Caching","Device-Pixel-Ratio Client Hint","highperformanceimages.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"emb